{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096671 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096458 :question/id #uuid "7b44089c-8ca7-57e5-b390-7900647e3884" :question/math-academy-id "e-4692" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations that is represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\left[\n\t\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3\\end{array} \n\t\\right].\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x_1,$ $x_2,$ and $x_3.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 3{x}_{3} &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n3x_3=3 \n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \n\tx_3=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(1)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 1$ and $x_2 = -3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x_1+(-3)-(1) = 0\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = \\dfrac{1}{2} (3 + 1) = 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 2,$ $x_2=-3,$ and $x_3 = 1.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 2,-3,1 \\rangle.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8197a43-64ec-57b8-b1f6-ff9620a7d86f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093513} {:answer/id #uuid "f66e0549-fa79-57be-a090-7daa7e6426b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093514} {:answer/id #uuid "01f74554-aef4-5806-966f-8726c1c1e688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093515} {:answer/id #uuid "0b30b3a1-b02a-5349-8604-74c9b16742f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093516} {:answer/id #uuid "767afba2-b10f-512c-89d3-c8fe22f7eb97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093517}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d0ce4428-7b3b-5989-b5e8-8d57a4360b63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093512}] :question/id #uuid "404549b9-30ad-5005-8ba2-0b875f83cd7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-10202" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix:\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "517c2b95-3278-5288-97a8-8f4ad7d12b85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-15,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236335} {:answer/id #uuid "58b90198-a181-5ca7-820a-0cb2ae4ad41b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-85,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236375} {:answer/id #uuid "782c23fb-f476-55a3-962b-c00da83d7887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-75,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236570} {:answer/id #uuid "9af36a41-8158-5002-b336-bc334832f54b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,-10,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236790} {:answer/id #uuid "b734756b-8742-55f6-b6ab-d04424db9104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-75,-10,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "782c23fb-f476-55a3-962b-c00da83d7887" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-75,40,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236570} :answer-field/id #uuid "746029b9-082c-5f33-9a0e-5b120cac1acc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5592cf72-9e61-50b5-9aec-b1921100f3dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-10204" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z &=10 \\\\ y+5z &=15 \\\\ -z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=5\\,⟹\\,z=-5.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+5(-5)=15\\,⟹\\,y=15+25=40.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-5$ and $y=40$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+2(40)-(-5)=10\\,⟹\\,x=10-80-5=-75.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-75,y=40$ and $z=-5.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-75,40,-5⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "603897b1-4a1d-5913-acb7-bb727537e7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236428} {:answer/id #uuid "86e751a8-5c2f-5932-a2ea-81d73e1e0410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-1,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236657} {:answer/id #uuid "9b68172b-23b4-5c0a-86bd-f06f58db0794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236791} {:answer/id #uuid "a453a509-aab6-55b5-ae2e-d64aef0bb03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236847} {:answer/id #uuid "c403432a-3ea4-55eb-ab6d-792922568851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c403432a-3ea4-55eb-ab6d-792922568851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237056} :answer-field/id #uuid "52d1bc13-92cb-59a3-8ae0-f4728f10c30b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f51fa541-69ba-512e-9b86-f9dbb4dce8b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-10203" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y+z &=8 \\\\ y-z &=-1 \\\\ z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny-0=-1\\,⟹\\,y=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=0$ and $y=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x-2(-1)+(0)=8\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{8-2}{2}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3$, $y=-1$, and $z=0.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨3,-1,0⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265751 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3055d150-0d1a-52cc-ae5b-19cf8e6d29d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263410} {:answer/id #uuid "691201ef-c6c5-5f63-bd11-a328b8a1fab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263903} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce178d8-2d62-5394-bb04-c7bad40fb652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263938} {:answer/id #uuid "efd4d4ff-2c77-5667-9e4b-111960f6c85c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265105} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e5cbd1-137f-5f8b-adf9-2abb641d4ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ce178d8-2d62-5394-bb04-c7bad40fb652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263938} :answer-field/id #uuid "8abbe911-bfc0-50db-9d21-a97d6d7ecc16" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "767893ce-f15e-5dc3-ac2a-90c7bba1c030" :question/math-academy-id "q-129604" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+y+2z &=-3 \\\\ y+3z &=0 \\\\ -z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=1\\,⟹\\,z=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(-1)=0\\,⟹\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n4x+(3)+2(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{-3-3+2}{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=3$, and $z=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "104bd80b-99be-5b60-b3c6-c1da8374be84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263151} {:answer/id #uuid "28b6438e-8a75-5a80-979c-65c88c4b6ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263351} {:answer/id #uuid "62bd08d1-d4b0-5b68-ab0e-8ee63de49e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263853} {:answer/id #uuid "9839face-b425-5c66-9922-80db2823f455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264309} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfdb6ec-d675-5431-8123-9f6401f69b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62bd08d1-d4b0-5b68-ab0e-8ee63de49e4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263853} :answer-field/id #uuid "46e711a8-d744-599d-a5cc-41ec4a239291" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a5bd3a7f-0603-5a94-9bbf-0a46b897e249" :question/math-academy-id "q-129613" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-3 \\\\ -{x}_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n-{x}_{3}=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=1.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-3-2=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=-5$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}-(-5)+4(1)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{-1-5-4}{2}=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=-5$, ${x}_{2}=-5$, and ${x}_{3}=1.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c98f24-c563-528a-a6fd-00fbf4db6789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263706} {:answer/id #uuid "74eb0c20-e6b1-5f0e-b5b5-bf0a4af84a4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264015} {:answer/id #uuid "75bb0fd9-7bb4-5f84-a347-a78a5992eff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264025} {:answer/id #uuid "9a053451-5add-5650-bcf7-5efdda715c4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-30 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264319} {:answer/id #uuid "c7cccac8-3863-5bec-bd18-3c0f78b98198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264748}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75bb0fd9-7bb4-5f84-a347-a78a5992eff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264025} :answer-field/id #uuid "e73fb32c-a004-5fbe-9c18-83ea40a2c949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86f65392-52cb-532d-9e01-57782fdc15f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-129615" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=7 \\\\ 2{x}_{3} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0193877c-1ccd-5276-b9e5-09b65801f01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,3,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339143} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1c9297-8467-595b-bdc0-d8097ac98404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-4,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339815} {:answer/id #uuid "a0330b8a-eef6-5686-a1a9-18be65748b1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,4,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340578} {:answer/id #uuid "dea8c28b-a5fd-5511-887e-2f25e7e67248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341106} {:answer/id #uuid "e0231c26-9b6f-5e2a-ac8e-51ddb757e3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0231c26-9b6f-5e2a-ac8e-51ddb757e3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-3,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341119} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc9b1b47-0c17-5478-b1a9-c7e848073796" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6ce04cb-fc7f-5c70-94bf-242e6df7387a" :question/math-academy-id "q-72980" :question/problem "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y-z &=2 \\\\ y+3z &=6 \\\\ -z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(3)=6\\,⟹\\,y=6-9=-3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=3$ and $y=-3$ into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n2x+(-3)-(3)=2\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(2+3+3)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=-3$ and $z=3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨4,-3,3⟩.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165ea2fd-41c0-5400-b24b-77486a19a825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339326} {:answer/id #uuid "67ae6eb0-f860-56b5-a08f-2f5623a97b3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340049} {:answer/id #uuid "bf55a7f8-3683-5adc-8cf6-442d5d29a568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340833} {:answer/id #uuid "ddecb468-7ba6-5116-8ff8-2b5e7fe02d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341099} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf0aed3-bba1-520d-802b-6e0413c2d5b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddecb468-7ba6-5116-8ff8-2b5e7fe02d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341099} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7e5e5a9-3bd5-5992-93ff-7ad964a75306" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341761}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41fa8809-57ef-578c-b39f-9d0b73e06f90" :question/math-academy-id "q-72981" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations: \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=2 \\\\ 3y+2z &=-1 \\\\ -z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n\n$$\n-z=2\\,⟹\\,z=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n3y+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}(-1+4)=1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-2$ and $y=1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(-2)=2\\,⟹\\,x=2+2=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=4$, $y=1$, and $z=-2.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "368d6f09-f86f-5a1f-934f-edb2ada2ecdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,\\frac{1}{2},1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339616} {:answer/id #uuid "4016e3b4-303c-5e7d-bc9c-f626ddc0e67a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,-1,\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339702} {:answer/id #uuid "5a087a29-e907-5bbd-8024-d1c0e3d6066a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339946} {:answer/id #uuid "7f49b16e-bca9-5992-802b-f9800e9b025a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340272} {:answer/id #uuid "b28c83dc-7bea-5c71-a4cc-8b4d73503adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2},-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a087a29-e907-5bbd-8024-d1c0e3d6066a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339946} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d72ac37-7d4a-57f8-a026-426aa0ba98f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341600}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6577a967-44f3-50e6-9603-cd6d17cab94e" :question/math-academy-id "q-72983" :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+z &=-1 \\\\ y+z &=1 \\\\ 2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that\n \n\n$$\n2z=1\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(\\frac{1}{2})=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=y=\\frac{1}{2}$  into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n2x+(\\frac{1}{2})+(\\frac{1}{2})=-1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(-1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=\\frac{1}{2}$, and $z=\\frac{1}{2}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}⟩.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries"}
